: 160 g + Seasonal Veg: 150 g\"}], \"estimated_intake\": {\"calories\": 1957, \"protein\": 86, \"carbs\": 267, \"fat\": 63, \"fiber\": 35}, \"is_current_day\": false}], \"roadmap_30d\": [{\"week\": \"Week 1 (Days 1\\u20137)\", \"phase\": \"Metabolic & Caloric Reset\", \"focus\": \"Strict adherence to designated mess portions and establishing daily hydration baseline.\", \"mess_strategy\": \"Adhere strictly to designated OR MESS portions; eliminate unscheduled fried canteen snacks.\", \"milestone\": \"Stabilize blood glucose, normalize digestive transit, and establish disciplined water intake.\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 2 (Days 8\\u201314)\", \"phase\": \"Glycogen & Work Capacity Fueling\", \"focus\": \"Complex carbohydrate fueling for BPET/PPT drills with post-PT protein recovery.\", \"mess_strategy\": \"Prioritize dal, eggs, and lean curries within 45 minutes post-morning physical training.\", \"milestone\": \"Enhanced muscular endurance, reduced post-drill muscle soreness, and sustained training energy.\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 3 (Days 15\\u201321)\", \"phase\": \"Body Composition & Muscle Recovery\", \"focus\": \"Accelerated fat oxidation or lean muscle accretion based on soldier\'s target category.\", \"mess_strategy\": \"Maintain portion discipline for staple rice/roti while maximizing fresh greens and vegetable curries.\", \"milestone\": \"Target weight adjustment of 0.8\\u20131.5 kg toward military SHAPE-1 authorization benchmark.\"}, {\"week\": \"Week 4 (Days 22\\u201330)\", \"phase\": \"Peak Operational Readiness & Consolidation\", \"focus\": \"Consolidation of 30-day nutritional adaptations and long-term habit institutionalization.\", \"mess_strategy\": \"Sustain balanced mess rotation; maintain light dinner 2+ hours prior to sleep.\", \"milestone\": \"Optimized power-to-weight ratio, peak 5km run speed, and sustained SHAPE-1 military readiness.\"}], \"optional_diet_plan\": [{\"item\": \"Hydration Fluid\", \"recommendation\": \"Minimum 3.0 Liters of clean water daily, paced across morning outdoor drills and evening recovery.\"}, {\"item\": \"Seasonal Fresh Fruit\", \"recommendation\": \"1 whole seasonal fruit (e.g. orange, guava, apple) during mid-morning break if available outside mess.\"}, {\"item\": \"Operational Electrolytes\", \"recommendation\": \"Coconut water or lemon water with a pinch of black salt during high-heat field or BPET endurance training.\"}, {\"item\": \"Night Recovery\", \"recommendation\": \"Ensure dinner is finished at least 2 hours before lights-out; 1 glass of warm milk or water prior to sleep if needed.\"}], \"sample_menu\": [{\"meal\": \"Breakfast (Friday)\", \"items\": \"Puri & Sabji: 150 g\"}, {\"meal\": \"Tea (Friday)\", \"items\": \"Aloo Bonda & Tea: 1 cup (150 ml)\"}, {\"meal\": \"Lunch (Friday)\", \"items\": \"Rice: 120 g + Chapati: 2 pieces (~60 g) + Mix Dal: 160 g + Mix Veg: 150 g + Seasonal Veg: 150 g + Kheer: 50 g\"}, {\"meal\": \"Dinner (Friday)\", \"items\": \"Rice: 120 g + Chapati: 2 pieces (~60 g) + Dal: 160 g + Chicken Curry: 150 g + Mutter Paneer: 120 g\"}], \"dietary_guidelines\": [\"Adhere strictly to authorized OR MESS meal timings and portion recommendations.\", \"Finish dinner at least 2 hours prior to lights out for optimal sleep and metabolic recovery.\", \"Prioritize protein-rich mess items (dal, chicken curry, paneer, eggs) immediately post-exercise.\", \"Avoid excessive fried snacks or processed confectionery from unit canteen.\", \"Maintain daily hydration discipline with at least 3.0 Liters of water.\"], \"recommended_items\": [\"Authorized OR MESS preparations: dals, lentils, and lean proteins for muscle preservation\", \"Complex carbohydrate portions (chapati, rice) calibrated to daily physical exertion\", \"Seasonal vegetables and salads from unit rations for vital micronutrients\", \"Daily scheduled hydration of minimum 3.0 Liters\"], \"limit_items\": [\"Excessive portions of calorie-dense fried snacks (pakoras, puris) beyond recommendation\", \"Refined sugar, heavily sweetened tea/coffee, and carbonated beverages\", \"Skipping scheduled breakfast prior to morning physical training\", \"Consuming heavy meals less than 2 hours before lights out\"]}','{\"title\": \"Corrective Conditioning & Caloric Expenditure Regimen\", \"focus_area\": \"Cardiovascular capacity, joint-safe fat oxidation, muscular endurance, and progressive load adaptation.\", \"goal\": \"Weight Loss\", \"exercises\": [{\"exercise\": \"Low-Impact Aerobic Conditioning (Brisk Walk & Interval Jogging)\", \"type\": \"aerobic_run\", \"sets\": 1, \"reps\": \"3.5 - 5.0 km continuous\", \"duration\": \"30 - 35 mins\", \"frequency\": \"5 days / week\", \"rest\": \"5 mins stretch cool-down\", \"intensity\": \"Moderate\", \"progression\": \"Increase duration by 5 minutes every 2 weeks toward 45 mins.\", \"notes\": \"Sustains optimal fat oxidation heart rate zone (60-70% max HR) without excessive joint impact.\", \"progression_note\": \"Increase duration by 5 minutes every 2 weeks toward 45 mins.\"}, {\"exercise\": \"Bodyweight Squats & Alternating Lunges\", \"type\": \"lower_body_strength\", \"sets\": 3, \"reps\": \"12 - 15 reps per set\", \"duration\": \"12 mins\", \"frequency\": \"3 days / week\", \"rest\": \"60 sec\", \"intensity\": \"Moderate\", \"progression\": \"Increase reps by 2 every 2 weeks up to 20 reps.\", \"notes\": \"Develops knee joint stability, quad endurance, and lower-body load carriage support.\", \"progression_note\": \"Increase reps by 2 every 2 weeks up to 20 reps.\"}, {\"exercise\": \"Cadence Push-Ups (Strict Form / Incline if Required)\", \"type\": \"upper_push\", \"sets\": 3, \"reps\": \"10 - 15 strict reps\", \"duration\": \"10 mins\", \"frequency\": \"4 days / week\", \"rest\": \"60 sec\", \"intensity\": \"Moderate\", \"progression\": \"Advance by 2 reps weekly toward standard 25-rep benchmark.\", \"notes\": \"Maintain neutral spine and 45-degree elbow tuck for shoulder preservation.\", \"progression_note\": \"Advance by 2 reps weekly toward standard 25-rep benchmark.\"}, {\"exercise\": \"Prone Plank Hold & Side Bridge Core Circuit\", \"type\": \"core_stabilization\", \"sets\": 3, \"reps\": \"30 - 45 sec front + 25 sec each side\", \"duration\": \"8 mins\", \"frequency\": \"4 days / week\", \"rest\": \"45 sec\", \"intensity\": \"Moderate\", \"progression\": \"Increase hold time by 5 seconds every week toward 60 seconds.\", \"notes\": \"Strengthens abdominal wall, transverse abdominis, and protects lumbar spine.\", \"progression_note\": \"Increase hold time by 5 seconds every week toward 60 seconds.\"}, {\"exercise\": \"Dynamic Joint Mobility & Flexibility Cool-Down\", \"type\": \"flexibility\", \"sets\": 1, \"reps\": \"Full-body static & dynamic stretches\", \"duration\": \"15 mins\", \"frequency\": \"Daily after PT\", \"rest\": \"N/A\", \"intensity\": \"Low\", \"progression\": \"Maintain full range of motion across ankles, hips, and shoulders.\", \"notes\": \"Prevents post-drill muscle soreness, stiffness, and joint fatigue.\", \"progression_note\": \"Maintain full range of motion across ankles, hips, and shoulders.\"}], \"blocked_exercises\": [], \"weekly_structure\": [{\"day\": \"Monday\", \"focus\": \"Cardiovascular Endurance & 5km Road Run\", \"session\": \"Morning Outdoor PT (06:00 - 07:15)\"}, {\"day\": \"Tuesday\", \"focus\": \"Calisthenics & Strength Conditioning\", \"session\": \"Unit PT Ground (06:00 - 07:00)\"}, {\"day\": \"Wednesday\", \"focus\": \"Tactical Obstacle Course & Rope Work\", \"session\": \"Morning Obstacle Track (06:00 - 07:15)\"}, {\"day\": \"Thursday\", \"focus\": \"Core Stabilization & High-Tempo Sprint Shuttles\", \"session\": \"Morning PT (06:00 - 07:00)\"}, {\"day\": \"Friday\", \"focus\": \"2.4km / 5km Speed Assessment Drill\", \"session\": \"Timed Speed Track (06:00 - 07:15)\"}, {\"day\": \"Saturday\", \"focus\": \"Unit Team Sports & Active Recreation\", \"session\": \"Evening Sports (16:30 - 18:00)\"}, {\"day\": \"Sunday\", \"focus\": \"Active Recovery & Dynamic Mobility 